as accepted.\n\n**What the DSKY showed at each checkpoint:**\n\n- **Reset (V36E):** display blanked completely after ENTR, including PROG. Reset accepted.\n- **Idle loop (V37E 00E):** PROG read 00 on the first attempt, with COMP ACTY briefly lit. No repeat was needed.\n- **Lamp test (V35E):** PROG, VERB, NOUN all lit 88 and all three registers lit +88888. Lamps seen lit during the test were VEL, NO ATT, ALT, GIMBAL LOCK, TRACKER, PROG, UPLINK ACTY, TEMP, STBY, KEY REL, OPR ERR, RESTART, and COMP ACTY. After it ended, PROG returned to 00, all lamps went off, and the 88s lingered in VERB, NOUN, and the registers.\n- **Clock (V16N36E):** two clean readings, both with R1 +00002 and R2 +00016.\n\n| Reading | R3 | Wall time |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | +01602 | t=71.3 s |\n| B | +04602 | t=101.5 s |\n\n  R3 advanced by 30.00 s over about 30 s of wall time, so the clock is counting.\n- **Gimbal angles (V16N20E):** R1 +00000, R2 +00000, R3 +00000, stable across two reads, consistent with an unpowered IMU.\n\n**Notes.** OPR ERR lit only as part of the lamp test and was off afterward, so RSET was never pressed. The first reads after keying V16N36 and V16N20 caught the registers mid-refresh from the previous contents. I reported those transitional values in the done report as read, alongside the stable readings. The gimbal-angle monitor was left running when the flight closed.","ttft_ms":1748,"type":"result","duration_ms":148386,"uuid":"90a422be-a3f4-4fff-a124-0427f19bb690","ttft_stream_ms":1471,"time_to_request_ms":18,"queued_turn_count":0}
